# Demo requests for the backend viva.
# Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao) and click
# "Send Request" above each one. Run them top to bottom: the login requests
# store tokens that later requests use.
# Replace Demo@1234 with your SEED_PASSWORD if you chose a different one.

@base = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@password = Demo@1234

### 1. Health check (public)
GET {{base}}/health

### 2. Valid request: list lessons (public)
GET {{base}}/lessons

### 3. Invalid request -> 400 with our standard error format
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "123", "role": "planner" }

### 4. Log in as student 1
# @name student1
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student1@gramshiksha.in", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 5. Log in as student 2
# @name student2
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student2@gramshiksha.in", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 6. Log in as teacher
# @name teacher
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "teacher@gramshiksha.in", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 7. Log in as planner
# @name planner
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "planner@gramshiksha.in", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 8. No token -> 401
GET {{base}}/results

### 9. Student token on a staff-only route -> 403 (wrong role)
GET {{base}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{student1.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. Student 2's own results
# @name student2Results
GET {{base}}/results/me
Authorization: Bearer {{student2.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11. Student 1 tries to read student 2's first result -> 403 (not the owner)
GET {{base}}/results/{{student2Results.response.body.$.data[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{student1.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12. Teacher: filtered, sorted, paginated list (watch the SQL in the terminal)
GET {{base}}/results?village=Bargi&sort=-score&page=1&limit=3
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13. Asking for a huge page -> 400
GET {{base}}/results?limit=5000
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14. Save a quiz result. Send it twice: 201, then 200 with "duplicates": 1
# (Recording again? Change the last digit of clientId to get a fresh one.)
POST {{base}}/results
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{student1.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "clientId": "6f1c2a9e-1b7d-4a3f-9c55-0d2e8b7a4c11",
  "lessonId": 1,
  "lessonTitle": "The Water Cycle",
  "village": "Bargi",
  "score": 2,
  "total": 2
}

### 15. Teacher tries to change stock -> 403 (planner only)
PATCH {{base}}/resources/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "delta": 1 }

### 16. Planner: +1 stock (atomic)
PATCH {{base}}/resources/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{planner.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "delta": 1 }

### 17. Stock below zero -> 422 from the database CHECK constraint
PATCH {{base}}/resources/3
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{planner.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "delta": -100 }

### 18. One school with its resources (one JOIN query)
GET {{base}}/schools/1

### 19. Security headers: look at the response headers
GET {{base}}/lessons

### 20. Wrong password: keep sending -> after 5 failed attempts you get 429
# (request 3 above also counted as one failed attempt)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student2@gramshiksha.in", "password": "wrong-guess" }
